Subject: [PATCH 04/29] Fix the 15 compile errors the first build found

@Volatile cannot be applied to a delegated property, so GpuGuard.alert drops it:
the state object is what makes the field safe to write from the watchdog's
thread and read from the UI's.

This project's Kotlin is older than the 'break and continue in inline lambdas'
language feature, so the watchdog's loop cannot break out of a synchronized { }
block; the running flag is read through a function instead and the loop body
moves into its own method.

ActionRow's last parameter is 'progress', not the click, so the two trailing
lambdas on the settings page landed on the wrong one and left onClick missing;
both now pass it by name. The alert composable needed the foundation imports
for padding, height, fillMaxSize and background.

Everything else in the guard compiled on the first attempt.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
